# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated capture + render artifacts (regenerable from demos/ + capture pipeline).
# Anchored at the harness root for the same reason /.kapi/ is: unanchored, they
# also swallow a demo fixture's own directory of that name, and a web app fixture
# keeps its static files in public/. Demo 04's English catalog was authored, added
# and silently dropped that way, so every take invented its own source strings.
/captures/
/out/
/public/
/sandbox/
node_modules/
.remotion/
*.log

# Isolated kapi state (own plugins/home, populated by `npm run setup`). Anchored
# at the harness root: an unanchored pattern also swallows a demo fixture's own
# `.kapi/`, which is where a real project keeps its voice profile, so a fixture
# authored with one was silently left out of the repo.
/.kapi/
